ne\" stroke=\"#f8fafc\" stroke-width=\"1.8\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">\u000d\u000a    <path d=\"m11 7 9 9m18-9-9 9m9 18-9-9\"/><path d=\"M15 16h5v-5m9 0v5h5m-5 14v-5h5\"/><circle cx=\"24.5\" cy=\"20.5\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#f8fafc\"/>\u000d\u000a    <path d=\"M7 28h12M7 41h12M9 28v4l8 5v4M17 28v4l-8 5v4\" stroke=\"#f1c65d\"/>\u000d\u000a  </g>\u000d\u000a</svg>\u000d\u000a"},"language":"FROG","metadata":{"author":"","automatic_versioning":false,"description":"Run this document. Three independent exact-i32 Increment chains perform one, two and three increments from -2, -3 and -4; each computes timeout -1. All three Waits receive Create directly. passed_0/1/2 are False only after their successful barrier passage. Destroy consumes a typed Record join of all three outcomes; it cannot run directly after Create. These chains use the verified composed Increment profile without claiming other numeric corridors.\u000a\u000aRendezvous : trois préparations indépendantes\u000a\u000aMode: execution. Profile: studio-draft. Capability: windows-x64/structured-program.\u000aExpected:\u000aprepared_0 (i32) = -1\u000apassed_0 (bool) = false\u000aprepared_1 (i32) = -1\u000apassed_1 (bool) = false\u000aprepared_2 (i32) = -1\u000apassed_2 (bool) = false\u000a","documentation_uri":"","name":"Rendezvous : trois préparations indépendantes","name_source":"document","program_version":"0.0.0.0","tags":["native","typed","resources","example"]},"storage":{"array_mode":"automatic","version":1},"title":"Rendezvous : trois préparations indépendantes"}
